  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Turn a raw periodic calcium-imaging trace (optionally ambient-subtracted) into curated beat-by-beat periods, a normalized mean ± SD overlay, and aggregated transient-morphology metrics (APD20/50/90, rise/decay, slopes, AUC), exported as XLSX, PNG and session JSON. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
